# Situation

Repo: claude-engineering-skills. All Claude API calls go through one seam, `scripts/lib/anthropic-client.mjs`, which has two transports chosen by `CLAUDE_BACKEND`: `sdk` (the Anthropic SDK; params are sent to the Messages API as given) and `cli` (spawns `claude -p` and maps the result back to the SDK shape). On the maintainer's machine `cli` is the ambient backend; CI runs the committed default, `sdk`. Call sites that never named a backend therefore ran on `cli` locally.

Pull request #360 (open) is the work under review; the commit below (`a4697858`, 2026-11-15) is its "throw and pin" step. It makes the `cli` adapter throw when a call passes `system`, `tools` or `tool_choice`, and moves the call sites that pass `system` onto a literal `{backend:'sdk'}` pin. The author states that the code at each moved site is otherwise unchanged, and a new merge-time gate (`npm run anthropic:pin:gate`) checks the pins. The PR has been through several audit rounds that concentrated on the throw semantics, the gate and the availability checks.

The default model sentinel `latest-haiku` resolves to `claude-haiku-5-5` at this date; `WORK_UNIT_LABEL_MODEL` defaults to it. The PR also touches the judge (model `latest-opus`) and a prompt-refinement script.

# The PR step

**Commit message of a4697858**

```text
fix(anthropic): throw and pin, and make the pin enforceable at merge time

The cli backend no longer routes an unserviceable call to sdk: a call passing
`system`, `tools` or `tool_choice` THROWS, whether cli was ambient or explicit,
and the remedy is a declared `{backend:'sdk'}` pin at the call site.

Why the first precedence was wrong. It mirrored `reconcileBackendWithBaseUrl`
(ambient coerces, explicit throws) on the reasoning that both are the caller's
intent against an ambient env choice. A `baseURL` names a DESTINATION the
operator chose, so coercing the transport still reaches it; `system` names a
billable CONTRACT the call site never made a transport decision about. Routing
on it let a param decide which meter a call bills, at run time, with nothing
committed recording which sites had moved.

A mechanical census found SIX unpinned system-passing sites, not four. The two
extra are shapes a by-hand read cannot see: `evolve-prompts.mjs` HANDS its
client to `llm-wrappers.callClaude`, which passes `system` (neither file is a
violation alone), and `solo-control-audit.mjs` FORWARDED the backend through a
variable while `runPass` passed `system` on every pass — a spend-bearing
harness whose rows are compared across arms, recording
`provenance.backend: 'cli(default)'`.

The gate is the load-bearing half. CI runs the committed `sdk` default, so the
throw can never fire there: a new unpinned site would ship green and break only
where CLAUDE_BACKEND=cli is set. `npm run anthropic:pin:gate` has Rule A
(file-local, mechanical, undeclarable-away), Rule B (a committed census, because
the handoff is invisible file-locally), and an `indirectPins` escape that is
verified by re-reading the named options function rather than trusted.

Pinned sites also needed a new availability question. `isClaudeAvailable()`
answers for the ambient backend and is `true` on a keyless cli install, so a
pinned site passed its gate and then threw `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY required` for a
backend nobody selected. `isClaudeAvailableFor(backend)` is the same oracle with
the backend as an argument; seven gates now ask it.

CLAUDE_CLI_STRICT_MAX_TOKENS is removed — a second routing dial for a param
whose being unmet does not change the answer, and meaningless once routing is
gone. Its negative control stays: a stale value must change nothing end to end.

- `npm run guards:preflight`: PASS, 36 steps, 2595 tests, 0 fail
- negative controls, all run: neutering the oracle fails 11/27; the seam
  swallowing the verdict fails 7/27; an inert scanner fails 6/27; a trusted
  indirect pin fails 4/27; a planted unpinned+`system` file turns the gate red
  (exit 1) and removing it restores green
```

